The structural equality is present in the residual, but the backend does not use it to reduce `applyIndex`. I’m adding two guarded pure-function simplification lemmas: under that exact canonical-tuple equality, index 0 is the stored integer projection and index 1 is the stored float projection. Their match domain is no broader than the equality, and I’ll machine-check the corresponding bridge-free fixed-semantics equations separately for Gate A.
