The combined run crossed the same expansion profile, so claim composition is not firing for the nested loop. I’m taking the contract’s sound route: strengthen the already passing inner theorem to characterize the loop-target cell exactly, prove it in a bridge-free definition, and only then use that theorem-backed exact rewrite in the outer proof.
diff --git a/smoke.py b/smoke.py
new file mode 100644
